  "description": "but your wallet said, \"No!\"?\nTime to lace 'em up and get walking, cowpoke. The Fuji Tahoe delivers\nhardcore hard tail performance, just like its big brothers, but keeps\nthe budget under four digits. It's easy, really. Just substitute custom\nbutted 7005 aluminum alloy frame tubing for X-Fusion metal matrix composite,\nthen carefully select the best choices in entry-level competition-worthy\ncomponents such as Shimano's Deore LX rear derailleur, Ritchey's forged\naluminum crankset and Rock Shox's Air Judy XC suspension fork.\n\nAnd if you've been hankering to try disc brakes on for size, you'll be\npleasantly surprised to find that Avid's Mechanical Disc brake performs\nnearly as well as hydraulic disks-but with none of the inherent complexity\nthat comes with compressing brake pads with pressurized fluid. You can\nalso dial the Rock Shox Air Judy XC's travel from an awesome 80mm to a\nwhopping 100mm to suit whatever your local terrain and personal riding\nstyle dictate.\n\nThe Tahoe is equally at home on the starting line of a muddy NORBA cross-country\nrace as it is on a high and dusty IMBA Epic Ride. But that shouldn't keep\nyou from tooling around the local park any time you feel like it.",
